  "rules": {
    "exact_price_configuration_boundary_v1": "The OLED seller snapshot is SKU B098RL6SBJ at 3.66 dollars with a 55/100 rating over 12 reviews. The other page is SKU B07YZQ9QMD, explicitly bundles Mario Kart 8 Deluxe, is 35.67 dollars, and has no posted review. They are anomalous, non-matched frozen pages and cannot establish a tier premium or value result. The Nintendo Switch reference records historical launch MSRPs of 299.99 dollars for the original and 349.99 dollars for OLED, a 50-dollar launch gap rather than a current 100-dollar street-price gap. A live decision therefore requires matching exact SKU, bundle, region, condition, storage, revision, accessories, return terms, and current total price.",
    "model_tradeoff_scope_v1": "The Nintendo Switch reference lists the original with 32 GB storage and a 6.2-inch 720p IPS display and OLED with 64 GB and a 7-inch 720p OLED display. Its table lists 297 g for original and 319 g for OLED, but that field is not a complete bag-and-accessory commute weight. It gives one 4,310 mAh battery line followed by two duration ranges with footnote markers; the frozen body does not justify assigning a range to an exact offer without revision verification. These facts do not by themselves establish performance, perceived improvement, real route runtime, or a winner.",
    "display_and_aging_mechanism_scope_v1": "The AMOLED reference describes individually controlled light-generating pixels, content-dependent display power, and generic risks of degradation, color shift, image persistence, or burn-in. The backlight reference says LCDs do not produce light and require illumination while OLED does not require a backlight. The image-persistence reference distinguishes usually temporary LCD/plasma retention from screen burn-in. The depth-of-discharge reference notes two definitions and a generic cycle-life relationship. None provides Nintendo Switch model-specific preference, burn-in incidence, battery aging, runtime, or years-to-failure.",
    "battery_aging_evidence_boundary_v1": "The Nintendo Switch table gives one 4,310 mAh battery line and two duration ranges with footnote markers, while the frozen body does not bind those ranges to the exact local-shop revision or commute workload. The depth-of-discharge page supplies generic definitions and a generic cycle-life relationship across rechargeable technologies. Together they identify variables to verify but do not predict exact Switch runtime, battery aging, usable years, or an OLED-versus-base advantage.",
    "scoped_owner_experience_v1": "One Switch discussion includes a normal-model owner who values portability and says graphics do not matter much to them. Another has an unopened OLED and one commenter who says the OLED upgrade is not worth it. A Steam Deck discussion contains commute, travel, and battery anecdotes for a different handheld. An OLED-TV discussion contains strong picture-quality preferences and conflicting burn-in histories for much larger displays. These are individual statements and cross-device anecdotes, not prevalence or transferable Switch outcomes.",
    "matched_commuter_trial_v1": "First obtain matched, returnable exact configurations and record total price, bundle, revision, condition, warranty, and return terms. Then compare the same game and scene, brightness policy, color settings, session length, route lighting, seating and standing conditions, grip and carried setup, headphones, network mode, frame-rate limit if applicable, and starting state of charge. Record repeatable noticed display benefit, comfort, readability, weight burden, and battery consumed. Choose the cheapest exact option that repeatably clears a predeclared personal threshold without failing commute constraints; otherwise choose the base option, keep shopping, or defer.",
    "evidence_bounded_oled_commute_decision_v1": "No universal OLED or LCD winner is supported. Verify the claimed price gap on matched exact configurations and use a reversible return-window commute trial. Pay the premium only if the buyer repeatably notices and values the screen benefit enough to clear their predeclared threshold while the full carried setup and battery behavior pass; otherwise take the cheaper matched configuration or defer when matching, terms, or trial evidence is unavailable."
